{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed: Gerrit 2343 merged at 21:45:28Z with `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, 0 unresolved\ncomments. Gerrit rebased on submit, so the merged commit on `origin/main` is\n`ae203145fa39a153c21b6cba8b25cb5679849ec9` (not the pushed `b76ffae4bd15`); the landed diff is\n+4/-0 to `AGENTS.md` and nothing else.\n\nClose is taking an extra step worth recording, because it is a real seam rather than a mistake.\nClosing through the MCP server is refused with \"no commit references it\": `attach_commits` for\n`ae203145fa39...` SUCCEEDS there (`attached: 1`, so the object is in the server's DB), but the\nclose precheck scans commits *reachable from HEAD* and the server-side root has not advanced to\nthe merge yet. Waiting ten minutes did not change it, and the recorded COMMITS event does not\nsubstitute for reachability in that scan.\n\nThe worktree HEAD *is* `ae203145fa39...`, so the precheck passes locally; the local close then\nstops on the plan-review close gate because the certified attestation is bound to the MCP\nserver's environment and reads as `foreign_key`/`unsigned` here. Resolution being used: earn a\nplan-review attestation in the local environment by running the same gate (`rebar review-plan`,\nno `--force`), then close locally with `--ref ae203145fa39a153c21b6cba8b25cb5679849ec9`. That is\nthe same gate, run where the evidence is visible — not a bypass. No force override has been used\nat any point on this ticket."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787954456348022802,"uuid":"50741dee-8ac6-4079-80a0-0da090378a39"}